draw: route render-transient scratch to the oxivgl allocator

The software renderer allocates a scratch buffer per draw op, every frame,
and frees it in the same call: draw-task descriptors, scanline masks (arc,
line, fill, border, triangle, rect-mask), box-shadow blur/mask buffers, image
mask/transform buffers, and the radius/circle mask cache. All of it goes
through plain lv_malloc/lv_free with no callback hook, unlike draw buffers,
which expose buf_malloc_cb. Once a runtime pool is registered LVGL's TLSF heap
is one fungible arena, so this scratch lands in PSRAM and the renderer reads
it per scanline.

These sites are routed to oxivgl_render_scratch_*, which keeps them in
internal DRAM. build.rs pins the number of allocation sites per file: a future
LVGL that adds a non-render allocation here fails the build rather than
silently half-routing.

Origin: 325d34c ("fix(mem): Keep LVGL render-transient scratch in internal
DRAM (#124)").

